.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH hon 1  "hon 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
hon \- Read manga in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhon\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read manga in your terminal
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "hon search"
\fBhon search\fR <\fIQUERY\fR> 
.PP
Search every source and print grouped results
.TP
<\fIQUERY\fR>
Title or part of one
.SS "hon download"
\fBhon download\fR [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] <\fITITLE\fR> <\fICHAPTERS\fR> 
.PP
Download chapters, e.g. `hon download "solo leveling" 1\-10`
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
Source to download from (default: the one with the newest chapter)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
File format (default: `format` from the config file, else pdf)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pdf
.IP \(bu 2
cbz
.IP \(bu 2
images
.RE
.TP
<\fITITLE\fR>
Title; must match one series exactly, or be the only search result
.TP
<\fICHAPTERS\fR>
Chapters: `112`, `1\-10`, `1\-10,15,20.5` or `45\-` (to the latest)
.SS "hon read"
\fBhon read\fR [\fB\-\-source\fR] <\fITITLE\fR> [\fICHAPTER\fR] 
.PP
Open the reader at a chapter (default: where you left off)
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
Source to read from (default: the one with the newest chapter)
.TP
<\fITITLE\fR>
Title; must match one series exactly, or be the only search result
.TP
[\fICHAPTER\fR]
Chapter number, e.g. `112` or `10.5`
.SS "hon repo"
\fBhon repo\fR <\fIcommand\fR>
.PP
Add, list or remove the repos sources are installed from
.SS "hon repo add"
\fBhon repo add\fR [\fB\-\-git\fR] [\fB\-\-key\fR] <\fIURL\-OR\-FOLDER\fR> 
.PP
Add a repo and pin its signing key
.TP
\fB\-\-git\fR
Fetch the repo with the machine\*(Aqs git (for private repos)
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<BASE64>\fR
The repo\*(Aqs minisign public key, for a repo without key.pub or to check its key.pub
.TP
<\fIURL\-OR\-FOLDER\fR>
An https:// URL of a repo\*(Aqs index.json or its folder, a local folder, or with `\-\-git` anything `git clone` accepts
.SS "hon repo list"
\fBhon repo list\fR 
.PP
List the added repos
.SS "hon repo remove"
\fBhon repo remove\fR <\fIURL\-OR\-NAME\fR> 
.PP
Remove a repo and every source installed from it
.TP
<\fIURL\-OR\-NAME\fR>
The repo\*(Aqs location as `hon repo list` shows it, or its name
.SS "hon source"
\fBhon source\fR <\fIcommand\fR>
.PP
List, install, update or remove sources; test and index plugin files
.SS "hon source list"
\fBhon source list\fR [\fB\-\-nsfw\fR] 
.PP
List the sources the added repos offer and the installed ones
.TP
\fB\-\-nsfw\fR
Also list sources marked NSFW
.SS "hon source install"
\fBhon source install\fR <\fIID\fR> 
.PP
Install a source from the repo that offers it
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The source\*(Aqs id, as `hon source list` shows it
.SS "hon source update"
\fBhon source update\fR [\fIID\fR] 
.PP
Refresh the repos and install newer versions of installed sources
.TP
[\fIID\fR]
Only refresh the repo this installed source came from
.SS "hon source remove"
\fBhon source remove\fR <\fIID\fR> 
.PP
Remove an installed source
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The installed source\*(Aqs id
.SS "hon source test"
\fBhon source test\fR [\fB\-\-lib\-dir\fR] <\fB\-\-search\fR|\fB\-\-chapters\fR|\fB\-\-pages\fR> <\fIFILE.LUA\fR> 
.PP
Run one function of a plugin file without installing it
.TP
\fB\-\-lib\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Where `require` finds modules (default: ../lib next to the file)
.TP
\fB\-\-search\fR \fI<QUERY>\fR
Run `search` with this query
.TP
\fB\-\-chapters\fR \fI<MANGA\-ID>\fR
Run `chapters` for this manga id
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR \fI<CHAPTER\-ID>\fR
Run `pages` for this chapter id
.TP
<\fIFILE.LUA\fR>
The plugin file
.SS "hon source index"
\fBhon source index\fR <\fIREPO\-DIR\fR> 
.PP
Write a repo folder\*(Aqs index.json from its sources/*.lua and lib/*.lua
.TP
<\fIREPO\-DIR\fR>
The repo folder, holding sources/ and lib/
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
